==English==

===Etymology===
Compound of {{compound|red|neck}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang|pejorative|lang=en}} An uneducated, unsophisticated, or poor caucasian person, typically used to describe residents (of any gender<ref>[http://www.hit-country-music-lyrics.com/redneck-woman-lyrics.html Country Music Lyrics New Country Tunes]</ref>) of the [[rural]] Southern US.
# {{context|slang|lang=en}} The nickname given to miners who wore red [[bandana]]s for identification during the West Virginia mine war of 1921.  <ref>[http://www.wvculture.org/hiStory/minewars.html West Virginia Division of Culture and History]</ref>

====Synonyms====
* [[cracker]]
* [[peckerwood]]
* [[white trash]]

====Derived terms====
* [[redneckish]]
* [[redneckism]]
* [[rednecky]]

